# Rust
/target/
Cargo.lock
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Trunk build output (pwa crate)
/pwa/dist/

# Vendored deps for offline Launchpad/PPA builds (regenerated per release) —
# not meant to live in git. `/.cargo/*` + a negation (not a bare `/.cargo/`)
# so `.cargo/audit.toml` — cargo-audit's actual config discovery path, see
# audit.toml's own doc comment — can be carved out and tracked; a bare
# `/.cargo/` would exclude the whole directory as a unit, and git doesn't
# apply negation patterns to files inside an already-excluded directory.
/vendor/
/.cargo/*
!/.cargo/audit.toml

# Same idea for the pre-populated cargo registry cache used to build trunk
# and wasm-bindgen-cli offline (see debian/scripts/prepare-offline-build.sh
# and debian/rules) and the vendored wasm32 rust-std component — all
# generated fresh right before a PPA upload, never committed.
/debian/build-tools/cargo-home/
/debian/vendor-rust-toolchain/

# trunk build output for the megatokyo-pwa Debian package (see
# debian/rules) — distinct from /pwa/dist/ above, which is trunk's normal
# dev-build output.
/debian/pwa-dist/

